K {"id": "Q04", "expected_answer": "Entry costs paid immediately before any card or space effects; cannot use later gains to pay entry. One card sends one Agent using one matching icon. No-icon card cannot be played on an Agent turn.", "source_references": "Main p9 / extraction 425–452", "novelty": "Entry legality and costs"}
S {"id": "Q04", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [482, 506], "pdf_pages": [9], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}]}
A {"id": "Q04", "answer": "A Plot Intrigue played before placing the Agent may grant resources that are then available for the entry cost. Resources from the played Agent card or destination, which occur only after placement, cannot pay that same cost. One card sends one Agent using one of its icons; it cannot send multiple Agents. A card with no Agent icons cannot be used on an Agent turn.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Player Turns entry-cost timing; Agent Turn: choose only one Agent icon; no Agent icons means Reveal only."}
B {"id": "Q04", "answer": "A legal Plot Intrigue played before placing your Agent can grant resources that pay the entry cost. Resources gained after placement from the destination or the played Agent card cannot pay that same cost; the entry cost must be paid immediately before resolving either. One card chooses only one Agent icon and sends one Agent. A card with no Agent icon cannot be used on an Agent turn; it can only be revealed.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Player Turns: Plot before placement; pay before effects; one Agent icon; no-Agent-icon restriction."}
